For orientation, $1\ {\rm eV}^{-1}
=\frac{\hbar c}{1\ {\rm eV}}
\simeq 1.97\times10^{-7}\ {\rm m}.$ An atomic length of order $10^{-10}\ {\rm m}$ therefore corresponds roughly to an inverse kiloelectronvolt. These are order-of-magnitude conversions, not precision spectroscopy.

