p.src:
The negatively charged pion has valence-quark content $\pi^-=d\bar u.$ Those quantum numbers can annihilate into a $W^-$, which can then produce a charged lepton and the corresponding antineutrino: $\begin{aligned}
\pi^-&\longrightarrow W^{-*}
\longrightarrow e^-+\bar\nu_e,
\\
\pi^-&\longrightarrow W^{-*}
\longrightarrow \mu^-+\bar\nu_\mu.
\end{aligned}$ The star reminds us that the intermediate $W$ is virtual. The second channel is the dominant one.

